; Faction character in a fight (docs/ALIFE_TACTICS_DESIGN.md section 5), read by sivol_tactics.script.
; Plain ASCII. Values are numbers or comma lists with no spaces.
;   press         chance that a fighter who is shot at in the open advances (find_cover_3/4) instead of
;                 backing into cover (situation 9); also scales the "enemy is reloading" push (M1)
;   patience      multiplier on the wait before going to look for a lost enemy (time_hide)
;   hold_k        multiplier on how long a chosen cover is kept (lcp.ttl)
;   rout_k        morale multiplier (0 = never breaks, higher = breaks sooner)
;   finish_downed 1 = goes to finish a downed enemy, 0 = leaves him alone
;   heal_fallback 1 = a hurt fighter with a medkit or bandage backs into cover to treat himself
;   mut_rout      1 = may break and run from mutants (ecologists only)
;   melee_k       butt strike / stab / kite chance multiplier (0 = never)
;   suppress      1 = pinned down by fire from an unseen shooter, holds cover for seconds
;   theft_react   how much a stolen mutant part matters, added to the step in sivol_part_claim (-9 = never minds, 2+ = ignores rank)
;   sidearm       weapon section given once at his first fight when slot 1 is empty and slot 2 holds a magazine
;                 weapon ("none" = never); sidearm_novice is the one for a novice; sidearm_ammo is the box that comes
;                 with it (16 rounds); sidearm_cond = lo,hi is the condition (worn: it may end up in the loot)
;   exempt        1 = the table is not read for this community at all (stock behaviour)
;   s14, s15      weighted cover algorithms for "enemy lost" (name,weight,name,weight...)
; An unknown community falls back to [stalker] (logged once).
; Live edit: fl sivol_tactics.set("stalker", "press", 1)

